! Initial-letter edits, read only when INITIAL_EDITS in
! Makefile.mod-desktop-hfst.am is 'regex' or 'both'. It is 'no', so nothing
! here is compiled in today.
!
! The alphabet must match editdist.default.txt. This previously carried c and
! s in their North Sami hacek forms, which Lule Sami does not use, and omitted
! ng, n-tilde, w, x and z, which it does.
!
! There is no uppercase block and no lowercase-to-uppercase block. Both used
! to be here, and both named symbols the alphabet does not declare -- it has
! no uppercase letters at all -- so neither could ever fire. That is the
! intended shape: uppercase makes the error model much larger and the speller
! slower, and the chance of misspelling the initial letter of a name is low
! enough that other error models drop it too. Sentence-initial capitalisation
! is handled outside the error model.
[
[ [a|á|b|c|d|e|f|g|h|i|j|k|l|m|n|ŋ|ñ|o|p|r|s|t|u|v|w|x|y|z|ä|æ|ö|ø|å] ->
  [a|á|b|c|d|e|f|g|h|i|j|k|l|m|n|ŋ|ñ|o|p|r|s|t|u|v|w|x|y|z|ä|æ|ö|ø|å] ]::20 
] ;
